WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.804
The second job is taking care of your people.

2
00:00:03.854 --> 00:00:08.420
People stay, and do their best work, for a manager who notices them.

3
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:13.579
Four habits. Listen and help: notice pressure, move what you can, follow up.

4
00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:17.652
Grow them: ask where they want to go, then find the stretch.

5
00:00:17.702 --> 00:00:22.742
Thank them: specific, by name, that week. Great job everyone thanks nobody.

6
00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:26.408
Trust them: hand over the decision, not just the task.

7
00:00:26.458 --> 00:00:33.399
And one line every manager learns: when someone mentions health, family, or leave, you adjust the load,

8
00:00:33.449 --> 00:00:36.182
and the leave office decides eligibility.

9
00:00:36.232 --> 00:00:40.866
Send it the same day, through Origami, and never ask for a diagnosis.

10
00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:47.653
For example: a lab technician says her mother is in and out of the hospital and she might need time.

11
00:00:47.703 --> 00:00:54.984
Her manager moves the two deadlines she has this week, sends the request the same day, and tells her he did.

12
00:00:55.034 --> 00:00:59.193
A week later she is back, and the team greets her at the door.

13
00:00:59.243 --> 00:01:02.654
This week: thank one person for one specific thing.

